        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(gateway): lock config mutation allowlist contract",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nGateway `config.patch` / `config.apply` mutations are guarded by an allowlist, but the contract was not locked in tests. A regression could silently widen or narrow which config paths agents may change.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a focused contract test suite that exercises both the allowlist guard and the real `createGatewayTool().execute()` path for `config.patch` and `config.apply`, so future edits cannot drift without failing CI.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior change for operators. Maintainers and contributors get a stable regression gate on gateway config mutation policy.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Commands\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/gateway-tool-allowlist.contract.test.ts --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\n- **Scenario:** Agent tool config mutation allowlist contract\n- **Before:** Allowlist behavior existed in `gateway-tool.ts` without contract tests on the execution path.\n- **After:** 16 contract tests pass, including `createGatewayTool` `config.patch` / `config.apply` forwarding and pre-RPC rejection of protected paths.\n- **Observed output:** `Test Files 1 passed (1)` / `Tests 16 passed (16)`\n- **Why sufficient:** Tests call the same guard and tool execution path used in production agent runs; no separate proof script required.\n- **Environment:** local Vitest via `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs`\n",
        "branch": "codex/gateway-config-allowlist-contract",
        "head_sha": "75ee0791196d9718bbece9a676d8de17e9d84618",
